{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01LYpx8Lfd94H1yL6qAjcGJH","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# SYMBOLS.md — Phase A: public symbol surface\n2\t\n3\tDerived mechanically from `nm -D` on both shared libraries.\n4\t\n5\t* C library: `c_src/build/libharvest-work-3eT73m.so`\n6\t  (built with `cmake .. -DCMAKE_POSITION_INDEPENDENT_CODE=ON && cmake --build .`;\n7\t  the library name is derived from the parent directory name by `CMakeLists.txt`)\n8\t* Rust library: `translation/target/{debug,release}/libmatrixsum_lib.so`\n9\t  (`crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]`)\n10\t\n11\tRegenerate with:\n12\t\n13\t```sh\n14\tnm -D --defined-only c_src/build/lib*.so   | awk '{print $2, $3}' | sort -k2 > /tmp/c.syms\n15\tnm -D --defined-only translation/target/release/libmatrixsum_lib.so \\\n16\t                                           | awk '{print $2, $3}' | sort -k2 > /tmp/r.syms\n17\tdiff /tmp/c.syms /tmp/r.syms\n18\t```\n19\t\n20\t## Defined (exported) symbols\n21\t\n22\t| # | symbol | C type / size | Rust type / size | C source | present in Rust `.so` |\n23\t|---|--------|---------------|------------------|----------|-----------------------|\n24\t| 1 | `init_array`                | `T` 0x7f  | `T` 0x5d  | `lib.c:45`  | YES |\n25\t| 2 | `expand_array`              | `T` 0x77  | `T` 0x40  | `lib.c:60`  | YES |\n26\t| 3 | `add_element`               | `T` 0x78  | `T` 0x68  | `lib.c:75`  | YES |\n27\t| 4 | `free_array`                | `T` 0x31  | `T` 0x2c  | `lib.c:88`  | YES |\n28\t| 5 | `process_flags`             | `T` 0x80  | `T` 0x1b  | `lib.c:95`  | YES |\n29\t| 6 | `calculate_matrix_checksum` | `T` 0x56  | `T` 0x43  | `lib.c:115` | YES |\n30\t| 7 | `matrixsum`                 | `T` 0x18c | `T` 0x13c | `lib.c:128` | YES |\n31\t| 8 | `matrix`                    | `D` 0x30  | `D` 0x30  | `lib.c:28`  | YES (`#[no_mangle] pub static mut matrix: [[c_int; 4]; 3]`, 48 bytes — identical size) |\n32\t\n33\t**Missing symbols: 0.** The symbol diff (name + `nm` type letter + size for the\n34\tdata object) is EMPTY. Text-segment sizes differ, which is expected (different\n35\tcompilers); only names/linkage/type must match.\n36\t\n37\tNotes:\n38\t\n39\t* Only `matrixsum` is declared in the public header `c_src/include/lib.h`, but\n40\t  all seven functions plus the `matrix` data object have external linkage in the\n41\t  C translation unit and therefore appear in `nm -D`. All of them are part of the\n42\t  ABI surface an external caller can reach via `dlsym`, so all of them are\n43\t  exported by the Rust crate and all of them are covered by the differential\n44\t  tests (see `CONFIGS.md`, `ERRORS.md`).\n45\t* `matrix` is exported as mutable data in both libraries. Tests write to it\n46\t  through `dlsym(\"matrix\")` in **both** `.so`s and then re-check\n47\t  `calculate_matrix_checksum` / `matrixsum`, which proves the Rust translation\n48\t  really loads from the global (no constant folding of the initializer).\n49\t* `DynamicArray`, the `FLAG_*` macros and `SIZEOF_INT` are compile-time-only\n50\t  constructs in C (a `typedef` and `#define`s) — they produce no symbols, so\n51\t  there is nothing to export. `DynamicArray`'s **layout** is part of the ABI\n52\t  (`init_array` returns a pointer to it); it is `#[repr(C)]` in Rust and the\n53\t  layout is asserted field-by-field in the tests.\n54\t\n55\t## Undefined (imported) symbols\n56\t\n57\tC imports: `malloc`, `realloc`, `free` (+ the standard weak\n58\t`_ITM_*`/`__cxa_finalize`/`__gmon_start__` glibc boilerplate).\n59\t\n60\tRust imports the same three allocator symbols — the translation deliberately\n61\tcalls glibc `malloc`/`realloc`/`free` via `extern \"C\"` instead of the Rust\n62\tallocator, so allocator-edge behaviour (e.g. `malloc(0)`, `realloc(p, 0)`)\n63\tis bit-identical to the C. All remaining Rust imports are libc / `libgcc`\n64\tunwinder / `std` runtime symbols:\n65\t\n66\t`_Unwind_*`, `__errno_location`, `__tls_get_addr`, `abort`, `bcmp`, `calloc`,\n67\t`close`, `dl_iterate_phdr`, `free`, `fstat64`, `getcwd`, `getenv`, `lseek64`,\n68\t`malloc`, `memcpy`, `memmove`, `memset`, `mmap64`, `munmap`, `open64`,\n69\t`posix_memalign`, `pthread_key_*`, `pthread_setspecific`, `read`, `readlink`,\n70\t`realloc`, `realpath`, `stat64`, `strlen`, `syscall`, `write`, `writev`,\n71\t`gettid` (weak), `statx` (weak), `__cxa_thread_atexit_impl` (weak).\n72\t\n73\t**0 missing / undefined non-libc symbols in the Rust `.so`.**\n74\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01BKEg3WjMYzasdUnF8hLuaZ","session_id":"8d463897-d2e4-446a-b9bb-aaf6d62cb9b1","uuid":"073d5eca-6f1e-4a97-8a9a-27b95d33452c","timestamp":"2026-08-28T03:38:14.052Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Adversarial C-vs-Rust divergence audit"}
