{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01Xb2YsE6gguy7xE6WTXYobY","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# ERRORS.md — Phase A: error-surface table\n2\t\n3\tEvery distinct rejection / error return in `c_src/src/lib.c`, found by grepping\n4\tfor `return NULL`, `return 0`, `return -1`, `if (!...)` guards and every\n5\tallocation-failure branch. There are no `assert`s, no error enums, and no\n6\texplicit range checks in this library — the entire error surface is\n7\tnull-pointer guards plus allocation-failure paths.\n8\t\n9\t| #  | function | trigger (the exact invalid input/condition) | expected C result | test |\n10\t|----|----------|---------------------------------------------|-------------------|------|\n11\t| E1 | `init_array` (`lib.c:47`) | `malloc(sizeof(DynamicArray))` returns NULL (struct allocation fails) | returns `NULL` | `e1_init_array_struct_alloc_failure` (not directly forceable through the ABI; covered by inspection + the E2 sibling path, and by the shared-allocator argument in `SYMBOLS.md`) |\n12\t| #  | `init_array` (`lib.c:50-53`) | `malloc(initial_capacity * sizeof(int))` returns NULL → `free(arr)` then return | returns `NULL` | see E2 |\n13\t| E2 | `init_array` | `initial_capacity` so large that `initial_capacity * sizeof(int)` (size_t, wraps) is still an un-servicable size, e.g. `SIZE_MAX/4`, `SIZE_MAX/2`, `SIZE_MAX`, `1<<62 - 1`, `usize::MAX/4+1` | returns `NULL` | `e2_init_array_data_alloc_failure` |\n14\t| E3 | `init_array` | `initial_capacity` whose byte product WRAPS to a servicable value: `initial_capacity = 2^62` → `2^62 * 4 == 0 (mod 2^64)` → `malloc(0)` succeeds → non-NULL array with `capacity == 2^62` and `size == 0` | returns non-NULL (NOT an error — the C does not range-check) | `e3_init_array_capacity_wraps_to_zero_bytes` |\n15\t| E4 | `expand_array` (`lib.c:61`) | `arr == NULL` | returns `0` | `e4_expand_array_null` |\n16\t| E5 | `expand_array` (`lib.c:66-68`) | `realloc` fails: `arr->capacity * 2 * sizeof(int)` is un-servicable (e.g. capacity `SIZE_MAX/8`, `SIZE_MAX/2`, `1<<61`) | returns `0`, and `arr->data` / `arr->capacity` are left UNCHANGED | `e5_expand_array_realloc_failure` |\n17\t| E6 | `expand_array` | `arr->capacity == 0` → `new_capacity == 0` → `realloc(data, 0)` (glibc: frees `data`, returns NULL) | returns `0` | `e6_expand_array_zero_capacity` |\n18\t| E7 | `add_element` (`lib.c:76`) | `arr == NULL` (any `value`) | returns `0` | `e7_add_element_null` |\n19\t| E8 | `add_element` (`lib.c:79-81`) | `arr->size >= arr->capacity` and `expand_array` fails (capacity 0, or capacity so large the doubling cannot be allocated) | returns `0`, `arr->size` NOT incremented | `e8_add_element_expand_failure` |\n20\t| E9 | `free_array` (`lib.c:89`) | `arr == NULL` | no-op, no crash (void) | `e9_free_array_null` |\n21\t| E10 | `matrixsum` (`lib.c:154-156`) | `init_array(2)` returns NULL (allocation failure) | returns `-1` | `e10_matrixsum_alloc_failure` (not forceable through the ABI: `init_array(2)` needs 16+8 bytes; documented + asserted never taken for all tested inputs) |\n22\t\n23\t## Generic FFI boundary cases also covered (Phase C)\n24\t\n25\t| # | case | covered by |\n26\t|---|------|-----------|\n27\t| G1 | NULL pointer to every pointer-taking entry point (`expand_array`, `add_element`, `free_array`) | E4, E7, E9 |\n28\t| G2 | Zero length / zero capacity (`init_array(0)`, then `add_element`, `expand_array`, `free_array` on it) | `g2_zero_capacity_lifecycle` |\n29\t| G3 | Oversized lengths — every power-of-two capacity `2^0 … 2^63` plus `SIZE_MAX`, `SIZE_MAX-1`, `SIZE_MAX/4`, `SIZE_MAX/4±1` through `init_array` | `g3_capacity_sweep` |\n30\t| G4 | One step past a range boundary: `capacity = 2^62 - 1 / 2^62 / 2^62 + 1` (the byte-count wrap point), `size == capacity - 1 / == capacity / == capacity + 1` for `add_element` | `g3_capacity_sweep`, `g4_add_element_boundary` |\n31\t| G5 | Out-of-range \"enum\" values across FFI: the library has no `enum`, but `process_flags` and `matrixsum` take `int` **flag** words. Values with no valid flag bit set, values with every reserved/high bit set, negative values, `INT_MIN`, `INT_MAX`, `-1`, `0x7FFFFFFF`, `0xFFFFFFF0`-style words are all passed and compared. `matrixsum` likewise gets `INT_MIN`/`INT_MAX` (signed overflow of `sum`, `sum * 0x10`) | `g5_out_of_range_flag_words`, `g5_matrixsum_extremes` |\n32\t| G6 | Corrupted/hand-built `DynamicArray` passed in from the caller (`data` non-NULL, bogus `size`/`capacity` relationship) — the C does not validate it | `g6_caller_built_struct` |\n33\t| G7 | `free_array` on an array whose `data` is NULL (`free(NULL)` is a no-op) | `g7_free_array_null_data` |\n34\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01BKEg3WjMYzasdUnF8hLuaZ","session_id":"8d463897-d2e4-446a-b9bb-aaf6d62cb9b1","uuid":"604b793a-4cc1-46d9-a725-68221282d501","timestamp":"2026-08-28T03:40:24.358Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Adversarial C-vs-Rust divergence audit"}
